Curtis stared at the polite uncertainty on the screen.
Same class. Same city. A liability and a possible key, just like he had filed at the bottles. Behind him, Mika pulled her cap brim down and pretended not to watch his face.
He thumbed the next line and did not send it yet.
On the fifth floor, the hunt had a new number in it.
Mikado Ryuugamine, still thinking Ikebukuro was something you could answer with good manners, had just been reached by the classmate who slept through lunch and walked out of school with two girls claiming him —
and Curtis Nightstar had to decide how much of Mika, Yagiri, and a missing head a small-town kid was allowed to carry before morning.
