Curtis stared at the period like it had a temperature.
Wow. Touchy.
He could hear the hallway in it — Anri at his desk, Rio on his other side, lunch asleep at a table two girls had wanted, a small-town kid watching the foreigner collect rooms in a city Mikado had arrived in first and still did not own.
Behind him, Mika shifted on the far bed.
Curtis kept his face easy and typed anyway.
The thread was live.
The jealousy was live.
And what do you want was still a better opening than Shizuo, Namie, or a Black Rider on the stairs.
He just had to answer without turning Mikado Ryuugamine into another person who would run toward a scar for the wrong reasons.
