Curtis let out a breath through his nose.
Good guy. Touchy. Still coming.
Behind him, Mika waited in a room Mikado did not know existed.
On the fifth floor, the liability had just agreed to be useful —
and Curtis Nightstar had to choose how much of the scar, the head, and the name Mika a small-town kid could carry without the whole city arriving at the elevator.
