On the other side of Ikebukuro, Mikado stared at the screen until the words stopped looking like a prank.
He found Mika?
He needs a place for her.
The missing girl Anri still carried like an unfinished sentence. The foreigner who slept through lunch and walked out of school with two girls at his shoulders. And now Curtis Nightstar had the one person who could put Anri’s eyes back on something other than him.
If he helped, he would be the one who made the reunion possible.
Not the boy standing in the hallway watching.
A hero in Anri’s eyes. Relevant again.
The thought was ugly. He had it anyway. He agreed anyway, because the ugly thought and the decent one could share a cab.
